[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive report:\n\n## End-Loop Marker System and Ralph Loop Implementation - Comprehensive Exploration Report\n\n### Executive Summary\n\nThe end-loop marker system is a file-based signaling mechanism that allows agents running within a ralph loop to request graceful termination of the entire loop. It uses `.claude/ralph-end-loop.json` as a marker file and is detected through bash command pattern matching during agent streaming output.\n\n---\n\n## 1. END-LOOP MARKER SYSTEM\n\n### 1.1 File Location & Schema\n\n**Path:** `.claude/ralph-end-loop.json` (relative to project root)\n\n**Absolute Path Function:** \n- Line 86 in `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/ralph.ts`\n- `END_LOOP_MARKER_PATH = \".claude/ralph-end-loop.json\"`\n\n**Schema (Interface):** Lines 95-99\n```typescript\ninterface EndLoopMarker {\n  requested: boolean;        // Always true when written\n  timestamp: string;         // ISO8601 timestamp\n  reason?: string;          // Optional explanation\n}\n```\n\n### 1.2 Core Functions\n\n#### `writeEndLoopMarker(rootDir, reason?)` - Lines 163-176\n- **Purpose:** Write end-loop signal to marker file\n- **Parameters:**\n  - `rootDir`: Project root directory\n  - `reason`: Optional string explaining why loop is ending\n- **Behavior:**\n  - Creates `.claude/` directory if needed\n  - Writes JSON with `requested: true`, current timestamp, and optional reason\n  - Used by both the `kspec ralph end-loop` command and signal handlers\n- **AC References:** @ralph-end-loop ac-cmd, ac-reason\n\n#### `readEndLoopMarker(rootDir)` - Lines 182-192\n- **Purpose:** Read end-loop marker file if it exists\n- **Returns:** `EndLoopMarker | null`\n- **Behavior:**\n  - Returns null if file doesn't exist (fails silently)\n  - Parses JSON and returns typed marker object\n- **Usage:** Called from two locations:\n  1. In `end-loop` subcommand handler (line 1047) to detect if in ralph session\n  2. In streaming update handler (line 1572) to get reason for logging\n- **AC References:** @ralph-end-loop ac-detect\n\n#### `clearEndLoopMarker(rootDir)` - Lines 198-205\n- **Purpose:** Delete marker file after loop exits\n- **Behavior:**\n  - Uses `fs.unlink()` \n  - Silently ignores ENOENT (file not found)\n- **Called From:**\n  1. Line 1339: Iteration start (reset state)\n  2. Line 1800: Loop finally block (cleanup on exit)\n  3. Line 1283: Signal handler cleanup (SIGINT/SIGTERM)\n- **AC References:** @ralph-end-loop ac-cleanup\n\n#### `clearStaleEndLoopMarker(rootDir)` - Lines 211-221\n- **Purpose:** Remove end-loop marker if older than 1 hour\n- **Threshold:** `STALE_MARKER_THRESHOLD_MS = 60 * 60 * 1000` (line 87)\n- **Returns:** `boolean` - true if marker was cleared\n- **Behavior:**\n  - Reads marker, checks age\n  - Clears if older than threshold\n  - Handles missing file gracefully\n- **Called From:** Line 1335 (iteration start)\n- **AC References:** @ralph-end-loop ac-cleanup\n\n### 1.3 Detection & Signal Routing\n\n#### `detectEndLoopCommand(command: string)` - Lines 237-240\n- **Purpose:** Pattern match bash commands for end-loop signal\n- **Regex Pattern:** `/\\bkspec\\s+ralph\\s+end-loop\\b/`\n- **Matches:**\n  - `kspec ralph end-loop`\n  - `kspec ralph end-loop --reason \"explanation\"`\n- **Does NOT match:**\n  - `kspec ralph end-iteration` (deprecated name)\n  - Partial matches like `kspec ralph` alone\n- **Usage:** Called in streaming update handler (line 1569)\n\n#### `extractBashCommand(update: SessionUpdate)` - Lines 246-289\n- **Purpose:** Extract bash command from ACP session update events\n- **Behavior:**\n  1. Checks if update is `tool_call` or `tool_call_update` event\n  2. Extracts tool name from multiple possible locations:\n     - `_meta.claudeCode.toolName` (Claude Code pattern)\n     - `_meta.toolName` (fallback)\n     - `name` or `title` field (last resort)\n  3. Verifies tool is Bash (handles \"Bash\" or \"MCP__Bash\")\n  4. Extracts `command` from input/params\n- **Returns:** `string | null`\n- **AC References:** Tool request handling for session events\n\n---\n\n## 2. RALPH LOOP COMMAND - Main Integration\n\n### 2.1 Command Structure\n\n**Location:** `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/ralph.ts` lines 1030-1894\n\n**Registration:** Lines 1030-1033\n```typescript\nexport function registerRalphCommand(program: Command): void {\n  const ralph = program\n    .command(\"ralph\")\n    .description(\"Ralph automated task loop and agent control\");\n```\n\n### 2.2 Subcommands\n\n#### `kspec ralph end-loop` Subcommand - Lines 1037-1070\n\n**Action Handler:** Lines 1041-1070\n- **Flags:**\n  - `--reason <reason>`: Optional explanation string\n- **Behavior:**\n  1. Initialize context (line 1043)\n  2. Check for existing markers (lines 1046-1047):\n     - `taskLimitMarker`: From task limit enforcement\n     - `endLoopMarker`: Existing end-loop marker\n  3. Write new end-loop marker (line 1050)\n  4. Detect if in ralph session (line 1053):\n     - If NO markers exist → warn (line 1057)\n     - If markers exist → success (line 1060)\n  5. Log reason if provided (lines 1063-1065)\n- **Exit Code:** Always 0 (success)\n- **AC References:** @ralph-end-loop ac-cmd, ac-reason, ac-noop-outside\n\n#### `kspec ralph run` Subcommand - Lines 1073-1893 (Main Loop)\n\n**Core Loop Structure:**\n\n1. **Session Setup (lines 1236-1248):**\n   - Generate session ULID\n   - Set `process.env.KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION = sessionId`\n   - Create session with metadata\n   - Log session.start event\n\n2. **Signal Handlers (lines 1274-1291):**\n   - SIGINT handler (line 1288)\n   - SIGTERM handler (line 1289)\n   - Both handlers:\n     - Log signal received\n     - Kill running agent\n     - Clear both marker files\n     - Exit after cleanup\n   - Uses Promise.finally() pattern for async cleanup\n\n3. **State Initialization (lines 1302-1310):**\n   ```typescript\n   let endLoopRequested = false;        // Flags end-loop signal\n   let exitReason: ExitReason | null = null;  // Why loop exited\n   let lastIterationCtx: SessionContext | null = null;\n   let lastErrorMessage: string | undefined;\n   const recentTaskRefs: string[] = [];\n   const sessionIterationMap = new Map<string, number>();\n   ```\n\n4. **Iteration Loop (lines 1320-1779):**\n   - For loop: `for (let iteration = 1; iteration <= maxLoops; iteration++)`\n   - **Per-iteration flow:**\n     1. Reset end-loop state (line 1334)\n     2. Clear stale marker (line 1335)\n     3. Gather session context (lines 1344-1352)\n     4. Process pending_review tasks (lines 1357-1376)\n     5. Check for task completion (lines 1392-1420)\n     6. Build and send prompts (lines 1428-1465)\n     7. Run retry loop for task-work + reflect (lines 1486-1699)\n     8. **Check end-loop signal (lines 1724-1728):**\n        ```typescript\n        if (endLoopRequested) {\n          info(\"Agent requested end of loop. Exiting gracefully.\");\n          exitReason = \"end_loop_signal\";\n          break;  // Exit iteration loop\n        }\n        ```\n\n### 2.3 End-Loop Detection in Streaming Updates\n\n**Location:** Lines 1514-1620 (Update Handler Registration)\n\n**Streaming Update Handler (lines 1514-1597):**\n- Registered once per session (line 1514)\n- Receives each ACP session update event\n- **For end-loop detection (lines 1565-1583):**\n  ```typescript\n  if (!endLoopRequested) {\n    const bashCmd = extractBashCommand(update);\n    if (bashCmd && detectEndLoopCommand(bashCmd)) {\n      endLoopRequested = true;\n      // Read marker to log reason\n      readEndLoopMarker(ctx.rootDir)\n        .then((marker) => {\n          const reason = marker?.reason ? ` (${marker.reason})` : \"\";\n          info(`End-loop signal received${reason}`);\n        })\n        .catch(() => {\n          info(\"End-loop signal received\");\n        });\n    }\n  }\n  ```\n- Sets `endLoopRequested = true` flag\n- Logs signal with optional reason\n- Non-blocking (async logging, doesn't affect stream)\n- AC References: @ralph-end-loop ac-detect\n\n### 2.4 Loop Exit Conditions\n\n**Exit Conditions (lines 1306-1328):**\n\n1. **Explicit end-loop signal** (lines 1724-1728)\n   - `if (endLoopRequested)` → `exitReason = \"end_loop_signal\"`\n\n2. **All explicit tasks done** (lines 1392-1404)\n   - `if (explicitTaskScope)` and all completed/blocked\n   - `exitReason = \"explicit_tasks_done\"`\n\n3. **No automation-eligible tasks** (lines 1407-1420)\n   - `!hasActiveTasks && !hasReadyTasks`\n   - `exitReason = \"no_tasks\"`\n\n4. **Reached max iterations** (lines 1782-1784)\n   - Loop completes without break\n   - `exitReason = \"max_iterations\"`\n\n5. **Subagent max failures** (lines 1372-1376)\n   - `!continueLoop` after pending_review processing\n   - `exitReason = \"max_failures\"`\n\n6. **Consecutive iteration failures** (lines 1769-1775)\n   - `consecutiveFailures >= maxFailures`\n   - `exitReason = \"max_failures\"`\n\n### 2.5 Cleanup & Wrap-Up\n\n**Finally Block (lines 1785-1869):**\n\n1. **Signal Handler Cleanup (lines 1786-1788):**\n   - Remove SIGINT and SIGTERM handlers\n   - Prevents double cleanup\n\n2. **Agent Cleanup (lines 1790-1794):**\n   - Kill running agent\n   - Null out references\n\n3. **Marker File Cleanup (lines 1796-1800):**\n   - Clear task limit marker\n   - Clear end-loop marker\n   - AC References: @ralph-task-limit ac-reset, @ralph-end-loop ac-cleanup\n\n4. **Environment Cleanup (lines 1802-1803):**\n   - Delete `process.env.KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION`\n\n5. **Wrap-Up Agent Spawn (lines 1805-1869):**\n   - Only if not dry-run and exitReason exists\n   - Uses exitReason to determine wrap-up behavior\n   - AC References: @ralph-wrap-up-agent-on-loop-exit\n\n---\n\n## 3. SESSION STATE & KSPEC_SESSION_ID\n\n### 3.1 Environment Variable\n\n**Name:** `KSPEC_SESSION_ID`\n\n**Set By Ralph:** Line 1242\n```typescript\nprocess.env.KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION = sessionId;\n```\n\n**Alternate Name:** `KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION`\n- Used by codex skill safety guard (mentioned in comment line 1241)\n- Not visible in test references but documented in comments\n\n**Cleared On Exit:** Line 1803\n```typescript\ndelete process.env.KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION;\n```\n\n### 3.2 Session State Files\n\n**Location:** `.kspec/sessions/{session-id}/`\n\n**Files Created:**\n- `session.yaml`: Metadata (lines 34, 57-61)\n- `events.jsonl`: Append-only event log (line 35)\n- `context-iter-*.json`: Iteration snapshots (line 84)\n- `budget.json`: Task budget (line 36)\n\n**Session Metadata Schema (types.ts lines 29-47):**\n```typescript\n{\n  id: string;              // ULID\n  task_id?: string;        // Optional current task\n  agent_type: string;      // e.g., \"claude-agent-acp\"\n  status: \"active\" | \"completed\" | \"abandoned\";\n  started_at: ISO8601;\n  ended_at?: ISO8601;      // Only when status != active\n}\n```\n\n**Session Creation (ralph.ts lines 1244-1248):**\n```typescript\nawait createSession(specDir, {\n  id: sessionId,\n  agent_type: options.adapter,\n  task_id: undefined,  // Will be set per iteration\n});\n```\n\n**Session Status Update (ralph.ts line 1883):**\n```typescript\nconst status = consecutiveFailures >= maxFailures \n  ? \"abandoned\" \n  : \"completed\";\nawait updateSessionStatus(specDir, sessionId, status);\n```\n\n### 3.3 Event Logging\n\n**Session Events (store.ts lines 284-316):**\n- `session.start`: When loop begins (lines 1251-1264)\n- `session.update`: For iteration progress, tool calls (line 1589-1595)\n- `session.wrapup`: After wrap-up agent completes (lines 1845-1852)\n- `session.end`: When loop finishes (lines 1874-1882)\n- `prompt.sent`: Before sending each prompt (lines 1468-1480, 1655-1663)\n\n---\n\n## 4. TASK START INTEGRATION POINT\n\n### 4.1 Current Task Start Handler\n\n**Location:** `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/task.ts` lines 1081-1220\n\n**Handler Signature:** Line 1082-1085\n```typescript\nmarkMutating(task.command(\"start <ref>\"))\n  .description(\"Start working on a task (pending|needs_work -> in_progress)\")\n  .option(\"--no-sync\", \"Skip syncing spec implementation status\")\n  .action(async (ref: string, options) => {\n```\n\n**Current Budget Check:** Lines 1116-1125\n```typescript\nconst sessionId = process.env.KSPEC_SESSION_ID || null;\n// ... check budget before starting\nconst budgetCheck = await checkBudget(ctx.specDir, sessionId || undefined);\nif (!budgetCheck.allowed) {\n  error(budgetCheck.reason!);\n  process.exit(EXIT_CODES.VALIDATION_FAILED);\n}\n```\n\n### 4.2 Where to Add End-Loop Check\n\n**Recommended Location:** After session ID retrieval and budget check, before task update\n- **Line ~1125:** After budget validation passes\n- **Before:** Line 1129 (task update)\n- **Pattern:** Similar to budget check - read marker, exit if present\n\n**Proposed Implementation:**\n```typescript\n// AC: @ralph-end-loop ac-task-start-check\n// Check if end-loop signal has been sent (blocks new task starts)\nif (sessionId) {\n  const endLoopMarker = await readEndLoopMarker(ctx.rootDir);\n  if (endLoopMarker?.requested) {\n    warn(\"End-loop signal detected - cannot start new tasks\");\n    process.exit(EXIT_CODES.VALIDATION_FAILED);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Functions to Import:**\n- `readEndLoopMarker` from ralph.ts (or move to shared location)\n\n**Exit Code:** `EXIT_CODES.VALIDATION_FAILED` (4)\n\n---\n\n## 5. TEST COVERAGE\n\n### 5.1 End-Loop Tests\n\n**File:** `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/tests/ralph/end-loop.test.ts`\n\n**Test Suites:**\n1. **\"Ralph end-loop command\"** (lines 13-85)\n   - Marker file creation\n   - Reason inclusion\n   - Warning when not in ralph session\n   - Detection when task-limit marker present\n\n2. **\"End-loop detection helper\"** (lines 87-108)\n   - Regex pattern matching tests\n   - Covers: exact match, with flags, partial commands\n\n3. **\"Marker file cleanup\"** (lines 111-138)\n   - Schema validation\n   - Timestamp validity\n\n4. **\"Signal cleanup\"** (lines 140-163)\n   - Static analysis of signal handlers\n   - Verifies SIGINT/SIGTERM registration\n   - Checks Promise.finally() cleanup pattern\n\n### 5.2 Session Tests\n\n**File:** `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/tests/sessions.test.ts`\n- Session creation\n- Event appending\n- Budget operations\n\n**File:** `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/tests/session-create.test.ts`\n- KSPEC_SESSION_ID injection\n- Environment setup\n\n**File:** `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/tests/session-scoped-task-claiming.test.ts`\n- Task session_id stamping\n- KSPEC_SESSION_ID propagation\n\n### 5.3 Hook Tests\n\n**File:** `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/tests/hooks/ralph-task-limit-guard.test.ts`\n- Tests task-limit marker blocking\n- Bash command pattern matching\n- Related to end-loop (similar marker system)\n\n---\n\n## 6. KEY FILES & LINE NUMBERS REFERENCE\n\n### ralph.ts (`/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/ralph.ts`)\n\n| Feature | Lines | Key Functions |\n|---------|-------|---------------|\n| Constants | 71-87 | END_LOOP_MARKER_PATH, STALE_MARKER_THRESHOLD_MS |\n| Marker Functions | 89-221 | writeEndLoopMarker, readEndLoopMarker, clearEndLoopMarker, clearStaleEndLoopMarker |\n| Detection | 224-289 | detectEndLoopCommand, extractBashCommand, detectTaskCompleteCommand |\n| Command Registration | 1030-1033 | registerRalphCommand |\n| end-loop Subcommand | 1037-1070 | Handler action |\n| run Subcommand (Main Loop) | 1073-1893 | Complete loop logic |\n| Session Setup | 1236-1248 | createSession, env setup |\n| Signal Handlers | 1274-1291 | SIGINT/SIGTERM with cleanup |\n| State Initialization | 1302-1310 | endLoopRequested, exitReason |\n| Iteration Loop | 1320-1779 | Main for loop |\n| Update Handler | 1514-1597 | Streaming output processing |\n| End-Loop Detection | 1565-1583 | Pattern match and flag set |\n| End-Loop Check | 1724-1728 | Break loop on signal |\n| Cleanup | 1785-1869 | Finally block and wrap-up |\n\n### session types & store\n\n**types.ts** (`/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/sessions/types.ts`)\n- Lines 20-21: SessionStatusSchema\n- Lines 29-49: SessionMetadataSchema\n- Lines 138-146: TaskBudgetSchema\n\n**store.ts** (`/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/sessions/store.ts`)\n- Lines 43-97: Path helper functions\n- Lines 111-141: createSession()\n- Lines 150-163: getSession()\n- Lines 175-202: updateSessionStatus()\n- Lines 284-316: appendEvent()\n- Lines 284-316: readEvents()\n\n### task.ts (`/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/task.ts`)\n- Lines 1082-1220: task start handler\n- Lines 1105-1150: Session ID setup, budget check, task update\n\n---\n\n## 7. AC REFERENCES & ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA MAPPING\n\n| AC Reference | Implementation | Line(s) |\n|--------------|----------------|---------| \n| @ralph-end-loop ac-cmd | end-loop subcommand | 1041-1070 |\n| @ralph-end-loop ac-detect | detectEndLoopCommand, pattern match in updates | 237-240, 1569 |\n| @ralph-end-loop ac-graceful | Break loop when endLoopRequested | 1724-1728 |\n| @ralph-end-loop ac-reason | Reason field in marker, logged | 1050, 1574-1577 |\n| @ralph-end-loop ac-cleanup | clearEndLoopMarker in finally | 1800 |\n| @ralph-end-loop ac-noop-outside | Warn if not in ralph session | 1055-1058 |\n| @ralph-end-loop ac-signal-cleanup | Signal handlers with cleanup | 1274-1291 |\n| @ralph-task-limit ac-marker-format | TaskLimitMarker interface | 77-83 |\n| @ralph-task-limit ac-reset | clearTaskLimitMarker | 1331, 1797 |\n| @session-creation-and-env-injection | KSPEC_SESSION_ID setup | 1242 |\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table: End-Loop Flow\n\n| Step | Location | Action | Output |\n|------|----------|--------|--------|\n| 1 | Agent code | Call `kspec ralph end-loop --reason \"X\"` | Bash command in stream |\n| 2 | ralph.ts:1569 | Pattern match bash command | Sets `endLoopRequested = true` |\n| 3 | ralph.ts:1572-1577 | Read marker, log reason | Console: \"End-loop signal received (X)\" |\n| 4 | ralph.ts:1724-1728 | Check flag at iteration end | Sets `exitReason = \"end_loop_signal\"` |\n| 5 | ralph.ts:1320 (loop) | Loop breaks | Exits iteration for loop |\n| 6 | ralph.ts:1805-1869 | Spawn wrap-up agent | Final cleanup and context capture |\n| 7 | ralph.ts:1796-1800 | Finally block | Clears both marker files |\n\n---\n\n## Critical Design Notes\n\n1. **File-Based Signaling:** Uses filesystem marker rather than process communication for resilience\n2. **Stale Marker Cleanup:** 1-hour threshold prevents old markers from blocking subsequent sessions\n3. **Signal Handlers:** SIGINT/SIGTERM use Promise.finally() for proper async cleanup\n4. **Streaming Detection:** Works with fire-and-forget event logging (non-blocking)\n5. **No Session Persistence:** Markers are ephemeral; session metadata is in .kspec/sessions/\n6. **Resume-Safe:** Task start already handles resume case (early return), so end-loop check needs session context"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ad0cc19 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 87281\ntool_uses: 13\nduration_ms: 69316</usage>"}]